{"text": "Emergency drain In case of a power failure, drain the water inside the drum before taking out the laundry. 1. Power off and unplug the washing machine from the A electrical outlet. 2. Open the filter cover (A). - TYPE 1: Gently press the top area of the filter cover (A) to open. - TYPE 2: Push down the latch of the filter cover (A) to open. A 3. Put an empty, spacious container around the cover, and stretch the emergency drain tube to the container while holding the tube cap (B). B 4. Open the tube cap and let water in the emergency drain tube (C) flow into the container. C 5. When done, close the tube cap, and reinsert the tube. Then, close the filter cover. NOTE Use a spacious container because the water in the drum may be more than expected. English 47 WWWW55000000DD__IIBB__DD GGlloobbaall--PPJJTT__WWAASSHHEERR--MMDD__EENN((FFAA))..iinndddd 4477 22002255//44//2222 1100::3311::1122", "source": "D:\\Study\\4_Forth Semester\\AI\\project\\MultiAgent_RAG\\data\\Front_Load Washer AI Ecobuuble 9Kg_user_manual.pdf", "page": 46}